-- Q516: Property Transactions: Basis [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 168(d)(1), the half-year convention treats all property as placed in service at the midpoint of the tax year regardless of actual acquisition date. For 7-year MACRS property using 200% declining balance, the full-year rate is 28.57% (2/7), but the convention halves it to 14.29% in year one. Both Petrov and Santiago receive the identical 14.29% first-year rate.
Wrong (A): The half-year convention is not month-sensitive; both taxpayers receive identical first-year rates regardless of when the property was acquired.
Wrong (C): The half-year convention does reduce the first-year rate by half; it does not affect only the final recovery year.
Wrong (D): The half-year convention does not pro-rate by quarter; that describes the mid-quarter convention under Section 168(d)(3), which applies only when more than 40% of property is placed in service in the fourth quarter.$EXPL$
