  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 1245, gain on disposition of personal property is recaptured as ordinary income to the extent of all depreciation previously allowed or allowable. The ordinary income portion equals the lesser of the gain realized or total accumulated depreciation, with any remaining gain treated as Section 1231 gain.
Wrong (A): Section 1245 recaptures up to the full amount of depreciation, not just gain exceeding accumulated depreciation.
Wrong (B): The 25% maximum rate applies to unrecaptured Section 1250 gain on real property, not to Section 1245 personal property recapture.
Wrong (C): Only the lesser of gain or depreciation is recaptured as ordinary income, not the entire gain regardless of depreciation.$EXPL$
