-- Q531: Like-Kind Exchanges [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 453, the installment method calculates a gross profit percentage (total gain divided by contract price) applied to each payment received. Harper''s percentage is 40% ($80,000 gain / $200,000 price) and Mercer''s is 20% ($40,000 gain / $200,000 price). Harper recognizes $20,000 gain on the $50,000 down payment (40%), while Mercer recognizes $10,000 (20%). The method matches gain recognition with cash receipt.
Wrong (B): The percentage depends on each seller''s gain relative to the contract price, so different bases produce different percentages — not a uniform 40%.
Wrong (C): The formula is gain divided by price, not basis divided by price; 60% and 80% reverse the calculation.
Wrong (D): The installment method applies regardless of whether a down payment is received; it is the default method for qualifying deferred-payment sales under Section 453.$EXPL$
