-- Q534: Like-Kind Exchanges [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 121, a taxpayer may exclude up to $250,000 of gain ($500,000 for MFJ) from the sale of a principal residence if they owned and used the home for at least 2 of the 5 years preceding the sale. The ownership and use periods need not be concurrent, and the exclusion can generally be used once every two years.
Wrong (A): Section 121 requires 2 of the last 5 years, not 1 of the last 3 years; this understates both the use requirement and the look-back period.
Wrong (C): The threshold is 2 years of ownership and use, not 3; requiring 3 of 5 years would impose a stricter standard than the statute provides.
Wrong (D): The statute does not require 5 continuous years; any 2 years within the 5-year look-back period satisfy the requirement.$EXPL$
