-- Q538: Individual Taxation: Income [easy/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 465, a taxpayer''s deductible loss is limited to the amount at risk, which includes cash invested and recourse debt but excludes nonrecourse debt where the taxpayer bears no personal economic risk. Webber''s at-risk amount is $80,000 (cash only), so only $80,000 of the $150,000 loss is deductible. The remaining $70,000 is suspended until additional at-risk basis is created.
Wrong (A): The at-risk rules apply to all taxpayers regardless of AGI level; there is no $250,000 income threshold.
Wrong (C): Cash is included in the at-risk amount while nonrecourse debt is excluded — this choice reverses the inclusion rule.
Wrong (D): The entire purpose of Section 465 is to distinguish recourse from nonrecourse debt; nonrecourse borrowings are excluded from the at-risk amount.$EXPL$
