-- Q539: Individual Taxation: Income [easy/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 469, passive losses can only offset passive income. Torres has no passive income, so the entire $45,000 limited partnership loss is suspended and carried forward until she generates passive income or fully disposes of the activity in a taxable transaction. The compartmentalization prevents taxpayers from using tax shelter losses to reduce tax on wages and portfolio income.
Wrong (A): Wages are active income, which is precisely the category that passive losses cannot offset under Section 469.
Wrong (B): Dividends are portfolio income, not passive income — Section 469(e) explicitly excludes portfolio income from the passive category.
Wrong (D): The TCJA did not repeal or modify the passive activity loss rules under Section 469; they remain fully in effect.$EXPL$
