-- Q545: Individual Taxation: Income [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 469, passive losses offset only passive income in the current year. Morrison''s $30,000 passive income from Activity A absorbs $30,000 of the $50,000 passive loss, leaving $20,000 suspended — wages cannot absorb the excess. Upon a complete taxable disposition of Activity B, all suspended losses are released and deductible against any income type including wages.
Wrong (A): Passive losses cannot offset wages or other nonpassive income in the current year under Section 469, regardless of income level.
Wrong (B): Having passive income is beneficial, not disqualifying — it provides a source to absorb passive losses, allowing $30,000 of the loss here.
Wrong (C): The $25,000 rental allowance under Section 469(i) applies only to active participation in rental real estate, not to general passive activities.$EXPL$
