  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 904(d), the foreign tax credit limitation is computed separately for two main baskets: general category income (most active business income, wages, and other income) and passive category income (dividends, interest, rents, and royalties). The separate basket system prevents taxpayers from cross-crediting excess credits from high-tax passive income against low-tax active income.
